  measurementNotes: 'Measured 2026-09-04 on a Radeon RX 6650 XT (Vulkan) with llama.cpp
    build 10775, over 16 labelled guard scenarios in the Reactive profile with structured
    output on. Valid-action rate is the share of decisions the package could dispatch;
    expected-action rate is the share that matched the hand-labelled correct action.
    Reproduce with Docs/Experiments/run_matrix.py.


    Fastest of the three and
    the right default for reactive NPCs. Weakest at conditional rules: it got none
    of the six two-condition scenarios right from the guide text alone, so gate the
    action menu with an IActionAvailabilityProvider rather than describing conditions
    in Model Instructions (gating took it to 5/6). Native thinking makes it restate
    the prompt instead of deciding.'
